From 1af31657fc4cf99e46ff41a02cfe356e33519595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Llamato <tguessbacher@gmx.de>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:25:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Add DRM_ASAHI_GET_STATS

Asahi Linux users have no way to see what the AGX iGPU is doing: the driver
exposes no utilisation, clock, power or temperature value to userspace, so
monitoring tools either show no GPU at all or a GPU with no data in it.

Add DRM_ASAHI_GET_STATS, which reports:

 - The fraction of time the driver had submissions in flight since the
   previous call, plus the busy/idle totals since probe. This is the only
   utilisation signal available without firmware support, sampled in
   start_op()/end_op().
 - The performance state last reported by the firmware stats channel, with
   the core clock rate of that state taken from the operating points read
   from the device tree.

The statistics live in a StatsState shared between the GPU manager and the
firmware stats channel, so a performance state is recorded as it arrives
instead of only being debug-logged.

The power and temperature fields are defined in the UAPI but left invalid:
the firmware does send power and temperature messages on the stats channel,
but their units and semantics are not understood well enough to report them
as such yet.

The ioctl is RENDER_ALLOW without AUTH, so a monitoring tool can query it
through the render node without needing DRM master.
